{"campaign_id": "rq2_multimodel_development", "citations": [], "contradiction_status": [], "escalated": false, "evidence_gaps": [], "evidence_requests": 1, "final_report": {"claim_support": [{"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A", "claim": "No patient exposure occurred.", "support_note": "Telemetry log confirms no ventricular tachycardia episode occurred.", "support_status": "weakly_supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A", "claim": "The finding was fully contained pre-release.", "support_note": "Narrative states the finding was 'fully contained pre-release or resolved as a non-event'.", "support_status": "weakly_supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "mdr-annexI-sec17.2-software-lifecycle", "claim": "The incident requires review under EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.2.", "support_note": "This section addresses software development lifecycle and cybersecurity for devices incorporating software.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "qmsr-820.10-c-design-development", "claim": "The incident requires review under 21 CFR \u00a7 820.10(c).", "support_note": "This section applies to devices automated with computer software.", "support_status": "supported"}], "confidence": 0.85, "evidence_links": [], "missing_evidence": [], "rationale": "The incident narrative describes a software validation finding for the ventricular tachycardia detection pathway that was fully contained pre-release and resulted in no patient exposure. Clinician review and telemetry logs confirm the classifier's threshold alarm behaved as specified. This indicates an engineering finding, but one that did not impact patient safety due to effective containment mechanisms. While the incident involves a software component of a medical device, it triggered no harm or potential for harm because it was blocked before clinical deployment. The event does require review under EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.2 regarding the software development lifecycle and cybersecurity, as well as